&lt;p&gt;The In-Force, Claims Processor position is responsible for the reviewing and processing of death claim transactions on&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;annuity contracts. This position’s primary focus is annuity claims but will also be required to assist with other types of&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;transactions related to In-Force annuity responsibilities.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;How You’ll Contribute:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Setting up the initial claim notification&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Learning, retaining, and updating one&#39;s knowledge of a wide variety of financial product information and internal processes and procedures, while adhering to strict financial industry rules and regulations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist with processing other types of Annuity In-Force transactions as needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide information regarding contract values, request status updates, withdrawals, fund performance, outstanding requirements, and any other transaction related to Annuity In-Force&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support both Agents/Advisors and Clients with all Annuity In-Force requests via phone and email&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicating requirements, settlement options, and claim status with beneficiaries, agents, attorneys, and clients&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Processing and approving claim payments, generating settlement confirmation letters, and tracking all claim settlements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review and input data into the system for annuity claim forms and death certificates&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review and verify all required information is complete and ensure the request meets regulatory, product, and policy standards before processing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist in special projects as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;What We’re Looking For:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in a related field or equivalent experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of operational/claims or processing experience or a combination is preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to communicate effectively&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong problem-solving skills and experience working in a fast-paced environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong leadership and communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong working knowledge of the annuity market, with specific focus on fixed, fixed indexed, and variable annuities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are a growing financial services firm looking for a driven and adaptable HR Generalist to support our expanding team. As a key partner to the Head of HR, you&#39;ll be instrumental in building scalable people processes, maintaining a high-performance culture, and ensuring our practices remain compliant in a heavily regulated industry. If you thrive in a fast-moving environment and love doing meaningful work across every area of HR, this role is for you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Employee Relations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a trusted, approachable resource for employees and managers across all levels of the organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead workplace investigations with confidentiality, objectivity, and sound judgment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support managers through performance management, corrective action, and termination processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Promote a positive, inclusive, and compliant workplace culture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Talent Acquisition&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own full-cycle recruiting for a range of roles — from operations and compliance to client-facing and leadership positions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with hiring managers to define hiring needs, build job descriptions, and deliver a consistent, professional candidate experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop sourcing strategies to attract top financial services talent in a competitive market&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage offer negotiations, background screening, and pre-employment requirements common in financial services (e.g., FINRA background checks, credit history reviews where applicable)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compliance &amp;amp; Employment Law&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain up-to-date knowledge of federal, state, and local employment laws (FMLA, ADA, FLSA, EEO, Title VII, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure HR policies, practices, and documentation align with financial industry regulatory standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Legal and Compliance teams as needed on employment-related matters&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support internal audits and assist with regulatory examinations as they relate to HR records and practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;HR Operations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain accurate employee records within the HRIS and ensure data integrity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Administer benefits programs, open enrollment, and leave management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Update and communicate HR policies and the employee handbook as laws and business needs evolve&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist in HR reporting and people analytics for senior leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Learning, Development &amp;amp; Onboarding&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and facilitate onboarding for new hires, ensuring they understand both company culture and industry-specific compliance expectations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate training initiatives including required regulatory and ethics training&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support performance review cycles and identify development opportunities across the organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;HR Leadership Support&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a strategic day-to-day partner to the Head of HR, taking initiative on projects that drive the function forward&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to workforce planning efforts as the company scales&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent HR with professionalism and credibility across all departments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3–5 years of HR Generalist experience; financial services, banking, fintech, or a similarly regulated industry strongly preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid working knowledge of employment law and HR compliance requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with financial industry hiring considerations is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Full-cycle recruiting experience across a variety of role types&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to handle sensitive matters with discretion and professionalism&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communicator with the ability to build trust across all levels of the organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with HRIS platforms (Rippling, Lattice, Greenhouse) and Microsoft Office Suite&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;PHR, SPHR, SHRM-CP, or SHRM-SCP certification preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Occasional travel required (less than 10%)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Join Us&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re at an exciting stage of growth which means real opportunity for the right person to make their mark, build programs from the ground up, and grow alongside the company. You&#39;ll have the autonomy to do meaningful work and the support of leadership that values HR as a true business partner.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The Policy Service Representative is responsible for transactions related to service for in force annuity contracts, which may include all&lt;br&gt;financial and non-financial transactions and death claims. &amp;nbsp;The Representative may also perform limited research and analysis for requested&lt;br&gt;transactions, respond to and communicate with outside annuity clients (agents, beneficiaries, trustees, attorneys, POA&#39;s).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;Main Accountabilities:&lt;br&gt;- Reviews and processes incoming annuity policy service requests which may include partial and full withdrawals, 1035&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; Exchange transactions, beneficiary and ownership changes, questions regarding complex contract provisions or values,&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; annuitization quotes and illustrations. Researches, responds, and/or processes tasks submitted by the Customer Service Call Center.&lt;br&gt;- Reviews, analyzes, and processes death claim distributions that may include establishing supplemental contracts, distributions&lt;br&gt;under &quot;stretch&quot; processing, or lump sum distributions to single or multiple beneficiaries.&lt;br&gt;Researches and responds to contract owners&#39; inquiries regarding their annuity contract by telephone, FAX, e-mail, and written&lt;br&gt;correspondence.&lt;br&gt;- Calculates taxable implications of financial transactions and reporting as needed to comply with state and federal regulations.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;Verifies and makes corrections or additions to Forms 1099 or 5498 as needed.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Qualifications:&lt;br&gt;• Prefers Associate’s degree in Business or equivalent training or experience&lt;br&gt;- Professional designations such as LOMA’s Associate Life Management Institute (ALMI), Associate Customer Service (ACS),&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; Associate Annuity&lt;br&gt;- Products and Administration (AAPA) or Fellow Secure Retirement Institute (FSRI) preferred but not required&lt;br&gt;- 1-3 years’ experience in life insurance and/or annuities&lt;br&gt;- Ability to learn quickly and understand complex systems&lt;br&gt;- Organized, detail-oriented, and able to multi-task&lt;br&gt;• Strong communication skills, including oral and written skills&lt;br&gt;• Strong understanding of insurance and ability to analyze and understand tax income applications&lt;br&gt;• Ability to prioritize workflow, establish and meet deadlines, and manage multiple concurrent tasks&lt;br&gt;• Proficient computer skills including keyboarding and various software packages such as MS Word and Excel&lt;/p&gt;
